<title>UK: UK card spending up 15.7 pct yr/yr in June - CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up 15.7 pct yr/yr in June - CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following consumer spending figures for June 1997 -</p>
<p>CARD EXPENDITURE (in million stg) *JUNE     JUNE 96  % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total	     8,230    7,111     15.7</p>
<p> Food and drink		    2,084    1,923	8.4</p>
<p> Mixed business		    627	522	 20.1</p>
<p> Clothing			    511	453	 12.8</p>
<p> Household			   683	564	 21.0</p>
<p> Motoring			    1,081    934	 15.8</p>
<p> Entertainment		     483	386	 25.1</p>
<p> Hotels				306	271	 12.9</p>
<p> Travel				914	818	 11.7</p>
<p> Services			    663	499	 33.0</p>
<p>NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months.</p>
<p>Credit Card Research Group economic adviser Peter Welsh said credit and debit cards were taking an ever larger slice of a burgeoning payments market.</p>
<p>&quot;In particular, the success of debit cards is remarkable. Only ten years after their launch they account for almost one fifth of retail spending.&quot;</p>
<p>London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
